From 8e061ebed9fd2964ca8dfc1f971f6675e0a88606 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mesh-LLM CI <ci@mesh-llm.local>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 02:46:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 35/56] skippy: clear stale sidecar rows before single-row MTP
 proposals

The native MTP sidecar keeps its own KV cache. When a proposal is
discarded, skippy_mtp_note_target_tokens only prunes the unverified rows
if the pending draft position falls inside the token window the target
just committed; the early-return reprime path and the out-of-window case
both reset the pending-draft bookkeeping and leave the rows resident.

The next proposal then resumes at session->n_past with seq_pos_max
already at or past that position, and llama_batch_allocr::init rejects
the batch. With plain RoPE this is tolerated, but M-RoPE requires the
batch to start strictly past seq_pos_max, so llama_decode returns -1 and
the sidecar surfaces 'llama_decode failed for MTP sidecar proposal'.

Clear the sidecar rows from session->n_past before the single-row
proposal loop, mirroring what the chained branch already does before
each of its decodes. Everything from n_past onwards is speculative by
construction, so the clear is safe whether or not the sidecar shares the
target's memory.
---
 src/skippy/speculative_decoding.cpp | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/skippy/speculative_decoding.cpp b/src/skippy/speculative_decoding.cpp
index 22bc61858..00ad16493 100644
--- a/src/skippy/speculative_decoding.cpp
+++ b/src/skippy/speculative_decoding.cpp
@@ -498,6 +498,20 @@ enum skippy_status skippy_mtp_propose_next(
         llama_seq_id * seq_ids = &seq_id;
         int8_t logits = 1;
         std::vector<float> proposal_h = session->mtp_pending_h;
+        // Drop any sidecar row at or past the position this proposal resumes
+        // at. The verify path only prunes a pending draft when its position
+        // falls inside the token window the target just committed; every other
+        // way a draft is discarded clears the session bookkeeping and leaves
+        // the unverified rows resident. Those rows put seq_pos_max at or past
+        // the resume position, and llama_batch_allocr::init then rejects the
+        // batch outright: harmless for plain RoPE, fatal for M-RoPE, which
+        // requires the batch to start strictly past seq_pos_max. Anything from
+        // session->n_past onwards is speculative by construction, so this is
+        // safe whether or not the sidecar shares the target's memory. The
+        // chained branch above already clears the same way before each decode.
+        if (llama_memory_t memory = mtp_ctx->get_memory()) {
+            llama_memory_seq_rm(memory, session->seq_id, session->n_past, -1);
+        }
         for (size_t depth = 0; depth < draft_limit; ++depth) {
             mtp_depth_scope.select(depth);
             llama_batch batch = {
